{"_id":"6a2feef12204ffbc59e5a2da","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"Sg5w8zO2Ji-uDJKEoWey9","description":"# Working with Strings\n\nPython provides a rich set of string methods for manipulating text: `strip()`, `split()`, `replace()`, `upper()`, `lower()`, `startswith()`, `endswith()`, and many more. These methods are applied directly to strings or through Pandas' `.str` accessor for vectorized text cleaning on entire columns.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"string ΓÇö Common string operations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/string.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebc5"},{"type":"article","title":"Useful String Methods in Python","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/useful-string-methods-in-python-5047ea4d3f90/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebc6"},{"type":"video","title":"String methods in Python are easy! πÇ░∩╕Å","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tb6EYiHtcXU","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebc7"},{"type":"video","title":"Python Tutorial for Beginners 2: Strings","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k9TUPpGqYTo","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebc8"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:24:17.420Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/Sg5w8zO2Ji-uDJKEoWey9.md"}